      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "float                4        IEEE-754 single precision, ~7 significant digits.\n\ndouble              8        IEEE-754 double precision, ~15–16 digits. The default for decimals in C.\n\nlong double        16        ⚠️ Second trap. On x86-64 Linux sizeof is 16, but the actual precision is 80-bit extended (the extra 6 bytes are padding). On Windows/MSVC it’s just 8 (same as double",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "float                4        IEEE-754 single precision, ~7 significant digits.\n\ndouble              8        IEEE-754 double precision, ~15–16 digits. The default for decimals in C.\n\nlong double        16        ⚠️ Second trap. On x86-64 Linux sizeof is 16, but the actual precision is 80-bit extended (the extra 6 bytes are padding). On Windows/MSVC it’s just 8 (same as double",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
