      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "size_t        8        Unsigned; the type sizeof returns and every length/count in the standard library uses. Always use it for sizes and array indices.\n\nptrdiff_t        8        Signed; the result of subtracting two pointers.\n\nintptr_t / uintptr_t        8        An integer guaranteed big enough to hold a pointer.\n\nwchar_t        4        Wide character. ⚠️ 4 on Linux, 2 on Windows.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "size_t        8        Unsigned; the type sizeof returns and every length/count in the standard library uses. Always use it for sizes and array indices.\n\nptrdiff_t        8        Signed; the result of subtracting two pointers.\n\nintptr_t / uintptr_t        8        An integer guaranteed big enough to hold a pointer.\n\nwchar_t        4        Wide character. ⚠️ 4 on Linux, 2 on Windows.",
